{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Iron with iron</b> — The bet in בברזל is drawn in place of two, and the meaning is \"before his friend,\" and the meaning of the bet is \"because of.\"" "<b>יחד</b> — Two roots: חדד and יחד. And anger of face is so called because wrath is seen in it, as we find פני ה' חלקם, and ופניה לא היו לה עוד, and its meaning is wrath and fury. The יחד is one who is angry, and the meaning of the verse is: a man sharpens the face of his friend." "<b>So too the meaning of iron</b> — Because of iron it is sharpened. And so a man יחד, because of the face of his friend — that is, he sharpens to contend with him because of his friend's wrath."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {2 "The last phrase reads 'his friend's wrath' but may be textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. The word חמות appears to mean 'heat/wrath' here, an unusual form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:06.239854425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}